  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 245 PM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nThursday and Friday...A couple of decent looking days look in store \nwith bouts of both sfc and upper ridging allowing for dry and near \nseasonable conditions.\n\nSaturday through Monday...The latest  suite of medium range models \ncontinue to suggest flattening flow again embedded with passing \nshort wave and associated sfc fronts making for a potentially active \nperiod.  First in line may be Saturday with a sfc front getting \nswept through the area off a passing LLVL cyclone along the \nUS/Canadian border. Then maybe a short lull for Sunday before signs \nof a digging longer wave trof acrs the western high plains arching \nsteering flow in a southwesterly fashion toward the upper midwest. \nThis could make for another unsettles period for Sunday night into \nearly next week if this pattern verifies.",
